SUMMARY:Scenic AVL Wildcard - Laurel Park - With AVL Camino Society
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the American
  Society of Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on the WN
 C Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/AVLCa
 mino/announcements).\n\nThis route starts with a five mile loop\, a coffee
  break\, and a figure eight. We will stop at Southern Streams coffee to ch
 at about Camino preparation and the experience of walking the different ro
 utes\, including the Frances\, the Norte\, and the Portuguese. If you are 
 unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are a few links to learn more:\n\n*[Amer
 ican Pilgrims on the Camino](https://americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory
 /western-north-carolina/)\n- [Stingy Nomads Camino](https://stingynomads.c
 om/camino-de-santiago-walking-guide/)\n*[Gronze Camino Planner](https://ww
 w.gronze.com/)\n\n**Distance:** This hike is made up of three sections\, a
 ll crossing the Ecusta trail. You can join and hike as much or as little a
 s you want. For those who are just starting their training\, come out for 
 half the distance!\n\n***9:30 am **- A five mile loop with a steep climb u
 p to Davis Mountain Road\, 3.0-3.2 mph\, also ending at Southern Streams.\
 n\n*** 11:00 am **- Southern Streams Coffee house\, near FCC church. 30 mi
 nute coffee break and camino chat. (if you want to sleep in\, meet us here
  at 11 ish)\n\n***Second Section: **Starting at about 11:30 am from Southe
 rn Streams coffee\, continue through lower Laurel Park. For those who want
  to exit\, you can return to the church on the Ecusta Trail for a total of
  about 7 miles.\n\n*** Last Section: **To downtown and St. James Church\, 
 returning via Ecusta Trail. 10.5 miles total distance. We plan to arrive a
 t the church around 1:15 pm.\n\n**Elevation Gain: **800 ft total if you do
  the full 10.5.\n**Pace: **3.0-3.2 mph\n**Surface: **Road\, with short str
 etch on gravel road.\n**Rating: **Strenuous for distance\, if you do the w
 hole thing.\n**Features:**\n*Neighborhood charm\, last of the spring color
 \, Hendersonville downtown\, St James church.\n*No bears. There may be gee
 se or ducks on Rhododendron lake.\n\n**Cautions: **There are a few stretch
 es on busy roads where we will need to walk single file.\n\n**Full Route: 
 **[Laurel Park Loop](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/laurel-park-loo
 p-improved-3937230?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n\n**Parking: **We are meeting at the Fi
 rst Congregational Church. Please carpool if possible.\n\n**Gear: **2L wat
 er\, snacks\, cash for coffee at Southern Streams.\n**Dogs: **On leash the
  entire time.\n**After Event: **Some of us will go to [ El Sol y La Luna\,
  ](https://maps.app.goo.gl/pfvgkMsJztNXAANi9)Cali-Mex\, after the hike.\n\
 n**Scenic Asheville Series: **This hike counts as a Wildcard substitute on
  my Scenic Asheville Series. There are 9 [hikes](https://docs.google.com/d
 ocument/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk) 
 in the series\; hike them all and receive an [attractive badge](https://do
 cs.google.com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit
 ) for your backpack. Check your status [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spre
 adsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).
 \n\n**On-Time Departure**\nWe will start by walking the labyrinth at the F
 irst Congregational Church\, so this is a pretty relaxed start.\n\n- Pleas
 e change your RSVP as soon as you know you can't make it.\n*If you have qu
 estions\, call the hike leader (Gracen) at 828-290-0886.\n\n**Guests:** Fo
 r this hike\, there are no guest restrictions. Bring them with you.\n\n**D
 isclaimer and Release of Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking on ci
 ty streets that may have traffic and/or hiking on natural surfaces. Partic
 ipants are responsible for their safety on streets and trails. The organiz
 er of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function 
 of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or particip
 ate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to
  assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as 
 a result of\, and associated with this event. You are responsible for any 
 guests\, dogs or other companions you bring with you. In addition\, you ac
 knowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/term
 s](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314367727
 /
